-- JSONDECODE reads a DATE, a TIME and a DATETIME in the forms TODATE, TOTIME
-- and TODATETIME read, and in the forms jl4-service's direct path read with
-- parsers of its own, among them the service's own answer for a DATETIME
-- (assumed, not ruled; review of #779, 2026-11-21). A string with anything
-- else after it is refused. TODATE itself is not changed.

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING DATE
`decode date` s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING TIME
`decode time` s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING DATETIME
`decode datetime` s MEANS JSONDECODE s

GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH AN EITHER STRING STRING
`zone of` s MEANS
  CONSIDER `decode datetime` s
  WHEN RIGHT w THEN RIGHT (DATETIME_TZ w)
  WHEN LEFT e THEN LEFT e

#EVAL `decode date` "\"2026-1-5\""
#EVAL `decode date` "\"2026-01-31T10:30:00Z\""
#EVAL `decode date` "\"2026-01-31 10:30\""
#EVAL `decode time` "\"1:5\""
#EVAL `decode time` "\"10:30:00Z\""
#EVAL `decode time` "\"10:30:15.5 UTC\""
#EVAL `decode time` "\"10:30:00+08:00\""
#EVAL `decode time` "\"10:30:00 Asia/Singapore\""
#EVAL `decode datetime` "\"2026-01-31 10:30:00 UTC\""
#EVAL `decode datetime` "\"2026-01-31 10:30\""
#EVAL `decode datetime` "\"2026-01-31T10:30:00.5\""
#EVAL `decode datetime` "\"2026-01-31 10:30:00 Asia/Singapore\""
#EVAL `zone of` "\"2026-01-31 10:30:00 Asia/Singapore\""
#EVAL TODATE "2026-1-5"

#EVAL `decode date` "\"2026-01-31xyz\""
#EVAL `decode time` "\"10:30:00 xyz\""
#EVAL `decode datetime` "\"2026-01-31 10:30 Asia/Singapore\""
#EVAL `decode datetime` "\"2026-01-3110:30\""
